Description: read-only V3D register module for vc4top (DKMS)
 vc4mon is a small read-only out-of-tree kernel module that exposes the
 VideoCore IV (V3D) register block under /sys/kernel/vc4mon/, so an
 unprivileged vc4top can read the same registers without /dev/mem.
 .
 The module does not register a platform driver, does not bind or unbind
 vc4_v3d, does not request_mem_region() and has no write path: every sysfs
 attribute is 0444 and all reads are 32-bit ioread32() loads.
 .
 Source is installed in /usr/src/vc4top-1.0.3 and built for the running
 kernel with DKMS.  Kernel upgrades rebuild it automatically at boot once
 the matching kernel headers are present.  Performance-counter sampling
 still requires root.

